GATE 1 — NO ACTION NEEDED.

Triage reports that this request needs no change. Its finding:
{{ .run_dir }}/evidence/no-action.md

Request:       {{ .run_dir }}/evidence/report.md
Run context:   {{ .run_dir }}/evidence/context.md
Evidence dir:  {{ .run_dir }}/evidence

This is the conclusion to be most sceptical of: it is also the
cheapest one for the agent that would otherwise have had to do the
work. Confirm it only if the evidence on disk shows it — that the
reported symptom does not occur, that it was already fixed and by
what, or that the behavior is deliberate and documented as such.

"I could not find a problem" is not the same as "there is no
problem". If triage did not look, send it back.

On `confirmed`, your reason is what the requester is told, and it is
the whole answer they get. Say what was checked, what was found, and
why no change follows.

Call submit_outcome with `confirmed`, `disputed`, or `needs_human`.